content.text:
Sonar finding: `validateDescriptor` cognitive complexity 17 > 15. Need to refactor.

Current function:
```ts
export function validateDescriptor(descriptor, registry): StructuralResult {
  for (const link of descriptor.lineage) {
    if (link.parent_version_id === descriptor.id) {
      return { ... };
    }
  }

  const counts = {...};
  const mergedParents = new Set();
  for (const link of descriptor.lineage) {
    counts[link.relation] += 1;
    if (link.relation === 'MERGED_FROM') mergedParents.add(...);
  }

  for (const relation of Object.keys(CARDINALITY) as ...) {
    const count = relation === 'MERGED_FROM' ? mergedParents.size : counts[relation];
    if (count === 0) continue;
    const rule = CARDINALITY[relation];
    if (count < rule.min || count > rule.max) return ...;
  }

  const continuation = descriptor.lineage.find(...);
  if (continuation !== undefined) {
    const parent = findVersion(...);
    if (parent !== undefined && parent.participant_id !== descriptor.participant_id) return ...;
  }

  return { status: 'VALID' };
}
```
Complexity: for(+1) if(+2?) Sonar counts nesting increments. Fixed by extracting helpers:

- `findSelfParent(descriptor): IdentityVersionID | undefined`
- `countByRelation(lineage): { counts, mergedParents }` or compute effective counts.
- `violatesCardinality(relationCounts): boolean`
- `findContinuationViolation(descriptor, registry): IdentityVersionID | undefined`

Then validateDescriptor becomes linear:
```ts
export function validateDescriptor(descriptor, registry) {
  const selfParent = findSelfParent(descriptor);
  if (selfParent !== undefined) return rejectRelation(selfParent);

  if (violatesCardinality(descriptor.lineage)) return { status:'REJECTED', code:'ERR_INVALID_CARDINALITY' };

  const continuationViolation = findContinuationViolation(descriptor, registry);
  if (continuationViolation !== undefined) return rejectRelation(continuationViolation);

  return { status: 'VALID' };
}
```
Complexity ~4.

Helpers:

```ts
function rejectRelation(parentVersionId: IdentityVersionID): StructuralResult {
  return { status: 'REJECTED', code: 'ERR_INVALID_RELATION', parent_version_id: parentVersionId };
}

const CARDINALITY_REJECTED: StructuralResult = Object.freeze({ status: 'REJECTED', code: 'ERR_INVALID_CARDINALITY' });
```
Careful: returning a shared frozen object is fine (immutable type). But `Object.freeze` typed? Could just create each time; no big deal. Sonar duplication? Creating literal twice not.

`findSelfParent`:
```ts
function findSelfParent(descriptor): IdentityVersionID | undefined {
  const self = descriptor.lineage.find((link) => link.parent_version_id === descriptor.id);
  return self?.parent_version_id;
}
```
`descriptor.lineage` readonly array; find available.

`relationCounts(lineage): { counts: Record<...>, mergedParents: Set<IdentityVersionID> }`:
```ts
function effectiveCounts(lineage: readonly DeepReadonly<LineageLink>[]): Record<LineageRelationType, number> {
