Let me consider effort for DFS memory fix:
Current collectPaths uses frames each with `edges` array copy and `visited` Set copy per branch → O(n²) for a linear chain. Rewrite with a single mutable `pathEdges` array and `visited` Set, plus a stack of iterators/frames:
```ts
function collectPaths(adjacency, scope, candidateID, originID): Path[] {
  const paths: Path[] = [];
  const pathEdges: LineageEdge[] = [];
  const visited = new Set<IdentityVersionID>([candidateID]);
  const stack: Array<{ node: IdentityVersionID; next: number }> = [{ node: candidateID, next: 0 }];
  while (stack.length > 0) {
    const frame = stack[stack.length - 1];
    if (frame.node === originID) {
      if (pathEdges.length > 0) paths.push(frozenPath(scope, pathEdges));
      // backtrack
      stack.pop();
      const removed = pathEdges.pop(); // edge leading to this node
      if (removed) visited.delete(removed.parent);
      continue;
    }
    const edges = adjacency.get(frame.node) ?? [];
    if (frame.next >= edges.length) {
      stack.pop();
      const removed = pathEdges.pop();
      if (removed) visited.delete(removed.parent);
      continue;
    }
    const edge = edges[frame.next]; frame.next += 1;
    if (visited.has(edge.parent)) continue;
    visited.add(edge.parent);
    pathEdges.push(edge);
    stack.push({ node: edge.parent, next: 0 });
  }
  return paths;
}
```
But origin handling: when frame.node === origin, we emit. On backtrack, pop pathEdges (the edge that led to origin). If candidate === origin initial frame, pathEdges empty → no emit; pop, pop pathEdges undefined. Fine.
`frozenPath(scope, pathEdges)` copies edges (map), so emitted paths independent.
Memory: O(depth) for pathEdges + visited + stack frames, plus output paths. Good. Deterministic.
Need ensure when frame.next exhausted, backtrack removes edge. Initial frame has no incoming edge; pop pathEdges undefined. Fine.
