Adjacency dedupe O(d²):
Current:
```ts
const edges = adjacency.get(edge.child) ?? [];
if (!edges.some(...)) edges.push(...);
```
Replace with `Map<child, Map<parentKey, edge>>` or Set of keys. Since edges are object, use `Map<IdentityVersionID, Map<string, LineageEdge>>` where key `${parent}\u0000${relation}`. Then convert to arrays sorted.
```ts
function adjacencyFor(...) {
  const adjacency = new Map<IdentityVersionID, Map<string, LineageEdge>>();
  for edge:
    if (!allowed || !reachable.has(parent)) continue;
    let byParent = adjacency.get(edge.child);
    if (!byParent) { byParent = new Map(); adjacency.set(child, byParent); }
    const key = `${edge.parent}\u0000${edge.relation}`;
    if (!byParent.has(key)) byParent.set(key, {...edge});
  const out = new Map<IdentityVersionID, LineageEdge[]>();
  for ([child, byParent] of adjacency) out.set(child, [...byParent.values()].sort(...));
  return out;
}
```
O(E) dedupe. Good.

