`consistent-type-imports` with default option prefers `import type` statements, but inline type imports are allowed? Default `fixStyle: 'separate-type-imports'` means it *prefers* separate imports and may report inline types? Actually `consistent-type-imports` default: `prefer: 'type-imports'`, `fixStyle: 'separate-type-imports'`. With inline type import `type Foo`, eslint reports error suggesting separate type import. So can't combine. That's why fixtures.ts has two imports from entities.js (lines 2 and 11) — and Sonar flagged S3863 in support/traversal.ts earlier for exactly that. Interesting: Sonar flags it, so fixtures has it too but maybe pre-existing lines not "new".

Alternative: avoid importing evaluateBinding into support. Instead put the `evaluateAt` helper in a new test utility file? Same issue. Could accept S3863... but Sonar gate is about duplication; issues also count toward "SonarCloud Code Analysis" check maybe quality gate on new issues. Earlier it failed due to duplication only? Gate showed only duplication ERROR. New code smells may not fail gate (sonar way requires A rating on new code, S3863 is minor → A still). But safer to avoid.

Option: use dynamic-ish approach? No.

Option: keep `evaluateBinding` calls in test files but factor the *arguments*: e.g. a support `candidateState` helper? Hmm.

Actually simplest: add helper in support but import evaluateBinding via `import { evaluateBinding } ...` AND move types into a `import type` — two imports same module triggers S3863 only for duplicate module import. We can avoid by not using types from traversal.js in that import block: put `evaluateBinding` in one import and the types in the same import as inline `type`... blocked by eslint.

Alternative: re-export types through a local `types.ts`? Overkill.

Alternative: define the helper in each test file? Doesn't reduce cross-file duplication.

Alternative: `evaluateAt` can take an `evaluate` function param? No.

Hmm, what about moving helper into `tests/support/evaluate.ts` importing evaluateBinding (value only) and types from `../../src/core/traversal.js` — same problem.

Wait: S3863 "imported multiple times" — we can avoid needing types by defining the helper's parameter types structurally, without importing traversal types? `BindingResult`, `ConditionalVersionBinding` needed. We could use `ReturnType<typeof bindingFor>` for binding and no return annotation (inferred). Graph/descriptors/assessments types can be imported from lineage/assessment/entities. So:

